Package: LukeFrameworkR
Title: Epistemic Uncertainty Quantification for Tree-Based SHAP Explanations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Luke", "Developer", email = "contact@insilicobiology.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Quantifies epistemic uncertainty in SHAP feature attributions for tree
    ensembles (randomForest, ranger, xgboost) using softmax tree weighting and
    Dirichlet hypothesis sampling. Computes standard deviation, 95% credible
    intervals, explanation entropy, and sign stability alongside ggplot2
    visualizations tailored for biological research.
URL: https://github.com/insilicobiology/LukeFramework_R
BugReports: https://github.com/insilicobiology/LukeFramework_R/issues
